# Images, Diagrams and Video
.image, .caption, .background and .video
9 Oct 2026

Ada Example
ada@example.com

## An image

With no size, an image fills the space left on the slide:

.image images/plasma.jpg
.caption A _plasma_ fractal made with [ImageMagick](https://imagemagick.org/).

## Image sizes

A fraction of the slide, or a height and width in pixels or fractions, with `_` for no limit:

.image images/shapes.svg 0.25
.image images/shapes.svg 120 _
.image images/shapes.svg _ 0.2

## Graphviz

A `.dot` file is rendered to the SVG file next to it with `dot`:

.image diagrams/pipeline.dot
.caption The worker pool from code.slide.

: present renders diagrams again whenever their source changes.
: Run present with -norender to show the existing SVG files instead.

## Mermaid

`.mmd` and `.mermaid` files are rendered with the Mermaid CLI, `mmdc`:

.image diagrams/run.mmd 0.7
.caption What happens when you click Run.

## A state diagram

With `-hot`, the browser reloads a presentation when its files change,
and shows parse errors over the old slides:

.image diagrams/hot.mermaid

## A background

.background images/background.svg

`.background` sets the image behind the whole slide.

## Video

.video video/testsrc.webm video/webm 270 480
.caption Made with `ffmpeg -f lavfi -i testsrc2`.
